## Savings Tracker v3 Notes

This project has moved from a prototype portfolio tracker to a richer local-first personal savings app.

### Implemented Direction

1. Keep the Expo managed workflow and existing Zustand persisted asset/history/settings data.
2. Add local-only savings goals and portfolio snapshots as additive persisted stores.
3. Restore Dashboard as the main control center with totals, rates, charts, goals, trends, and recent activity.
4. Keep Assets focused on fast entry and management with search, filters, sort controls, type totals, confirm delete, and undo.
5. Add full History and Goals tabs.
6. Upgrade backup/export flows with JSON import/export and CSV exports.
7. Keep UI theme-driven, accessible, and friendly to web, Android, and iOS.

### Verification Gate

Run these before considering a v3 change complete:

```bash
npm run typecheck
npm run lint
npm run test -- --runInBand
npx expo install --check
```

Also smoke-test the web app across Dashboard, Assets, History, Goals, and Settings in light and dark theme.
